## LAYOUT FUNDAMENTALS
VStack and HStack are the only layout containers — all slide structure is built by nesting them.
  A VStack with backgroundColor, padding, and borderRadius is a card; nesting stacks is how you create any visual grouping.
  VStack: children flow top to bottom. Main axis = vertical, cross axis = horizontal.
  HStack: children flow left to right. Main axis = horizontal, cross axis = vertical.
Layout properties (VStack and HStack only):
  gap: space between children along the main axis (not before first or after last).
  alignItems: position children on the CROSS axis (start|center|end|stretch). Default stretch.
  justifyContent: distribute children along the MAIN axis (start|center|end|spaceBetween).
Common properties (all nodes including VStack/HStack):
  padding: inner space between a node's edge and its content.
  margin: outer space pushing a node away from its siblings.
  grow: flex-grow ratio — how siblings split remaining main-axis space.

